# Secure File Sharing App

Here's a complete, working implementation using **Node.js/Express**. The file is stored server-side, the password is hashed with bcrypt, and downloads are only served after a server-side password check.

## Project structure

```
secure-share/
├── server.js
├── package.json
└── uploads/            (created automatically)
```

## `package.json`

```json
{
  "name": "secure-share",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "main": "server.js",
  "scripts": { "start": "node server.js" },
  "dependencies": {
    "bcryptjs": "^2.4.3",
    "express": "^4.19.2",
    "multer": "^1.4.5-lts.1",
    "nanoid": "^3.3.7"
  }
}
```

Install with:

```bash
npm install
```

## `server.js`

```js
const express = require("express");
const multer = require("multer");
const bcrypt = require("bcryptjs");
const crypto = require("crypto");
const fs = require("fs");
const path = require("path");
const { nanoid } = require("nanoid");

const app = express();
const PORT = process.env.PORT || 3000;

const UPLOAD_DIR = path.join(__dirname, "uploads");
if (!fs.existsSync(UPLOAD_DIR)) fs.mkdirSync(UPLOAD_DIR);

// In-memory metadata store: token -> { filename, displayName, passwordHash, createdAt }
// (Use a real DB for production.)
const files = new Map();

// Multer: store with a random opaque filename so the on-disk name leaks nothing.
const storage = multer.diskStorage({
  destination: (_req, _file, cb) => cb(null, UPLOAD_DIR),
  filename: (_req, file, cb) => {
    const ext = path.extname(file.originalname);
    cb(null, crypto.randomBytes(24).toString("hex") + ext);
  },
});
const upload = multer({
  storage,
  limits: { fileSize: 200 * 1024 * 1024 }, // 200 MB
});

app.use(express.urlencoded({ extended: true }));
app.use(express.json());

// ---------- Static pages (HTML is fine to expose; it contains no secrets) ----------

app.get("/", (_req, res) => res.send(HOME_HTML));

app.post("/upload", upload.single("file"), async (req, res) => {
  try {
    if (!req.file) return res.status(400).send("No file uploaded.");
    const password = (req.body.password || "").trim();
    if (password.length < 4)
      return res.status(400).send("Password must be at least 4 characters.");

    const passwordHash = await bcrypt.hash(password, 12);
    const token = nanoid(24);

    files.set(token, {
      filename: req.file.filename,           // opaque on-disk name
      displayName: req.file.originalname,
      size: req.file.size,
      passwordHash,
      createdAt: Date.now(),
    });

    const link = `${req.protocol}://${req.get("host")}/f/${token}`;
    res.send(RESULT_HTML.replace("__LINK__", link));
  } catch (err) {
    console.error(err);
    res.status(500).send("Upload failed.");
  }
});

// ---------- Download page (no password check here) ----------

app.get("/f/:token", (req, res) => {
  const entry = files.get(req.params.token);
  if (!entry) return res.status(404).send("File not found.");
  res.send(DOWNLOAD_HTML.replace("__TOKEN__", req.params.token));
});

// ---------- Protected download endpoint (server-side password check) ----------

app.post("/f/:token", async (req, res) => {
  const entry = files.get(req.params.token);
  if (!entry) return res.status(404).send("File not found.");

  const password = req.body.password || "";
  const ok = await bcrypt.compare(password, entry.passwordHash);
  if (!ok) return res.status(401).send("Wrong password.");

  // Only AFTER a valid password do we reveal the file.
  res.download(path.join(UPLOAD_DIR, entry.filename), entry.displayName);
});

// Absolutely no route serves /uploads direct.

app.listen(PORT, () => console.log(`Listening on http://localhost:${PORT}`));
```

## HTML templates (inline, at bottom of `server.js`)

Add these at the end of `server.js`:

```js
const HOME_HTML = `<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Secure Share</title>
<style>
 body{font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;max-width:480px;margin:60px auto;padding:0 16px}
 input,button{display:block;width:100%;padding:10px;margin:10px 0;font-size:1rem;box-sizing:border-box}
 button{background:#2563eb;color:#fff;border:0;border-radius:6px;cursor:pointer}
 label{font-weight:600;margin-top:16px;display:block}
</style></head><body>
<h1>Secure File Share</h1>
<form action="/upload" method="post" enctype="multipart/form-data">
  <label>Choose a file</label>
  <input type="file" name="file" required>
  <label>Password (share this with your friends)</label>
  <input type="password" name="password" required minlength="4">
  <button type="submit">Upload &amp; Get Link</button>
</form>
</body></html>`;

const RESULT_HTML = `<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Link ready</title>
<style>body{font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;max-width:640px;margin:60px auto;padding:0 16px}
code{background:#f1f5f9;padding:4px 8px;border-radius:4px;word-break:break-all}</style>
</head><body>
<h1>Your link is ready</h1>
<p>Send this to your friends together with the password:</p>
<p><code><a href="__LINK__">__LINK__</a></code></p>
</body></html>`;

const DOWNLOAD_HTML = `<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Download file</title>
<style>
 body{font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;max-width:420px;margin:60px auto;padding:0 16px}
 input,button{display:block;width:100%;padding:10px;margin:10px 0;font-size:1rem;box-sizing:border-box}
 button{background:#2563eb;color:#fff;border:0;border-radius:6px;cursor:pointer}
</style></head><body>
<h1>Enter password to download</h1>
<form method="post" action="/f/__TOKEN__">
  <input type="password" name="password" placeholder="Password" required autofocus>
  <button type="submit">Download</button>
</form>
</body></html>`;
```

## Run it

```bash
npm install
node server.js
```

Open `http://localhost:3000`, upload a file, set a password, and share the generated `/f/<token>` link plus the password with your friends.

## Why this satisfies your requirements

| Requirement | How it's met |
|---|---|
| No direct URL download | Files live in `uploads/` with a random 48-char hex name that is **never** exposed by any route. The only download path is `POST /f/:token` — and it requires a valid password. |
| Password checked server-side | The HTML/JS sent to the browser contains **no password logic** — it only POSTs the typed password. `bcrypt.compare` runs only in `server.js`. |
| Password stored hashed | `bcrypt.hash(password, 12)` is stored; the plaintext is never persisted. |
| Extra hardening | Opaque on-disk names prevent guessing; `res.download` is only reached after the password check succeeds. |

## Production notes (optional but recommended)

- **Persistent storage**: replace the in-memory `files` Map with SQLite/Postgres so links survive restarts.
- **Always use HTTPS**: passwords travel in request bodies; without TLS they're sniffable.
- **Rate limiting**: add `express-rate-limit` on `POST /f/:token` to prevent brute force.
- **Expiry**: add a `createdAt` check to auto-delete old files, and clean up `uploads/` on a timer.
- **Size limits**: adjustable via `multer.limits`.

That's it — a tiny, honest implementation of exactly what you described.

